"Making a dungeon needs a large area, abundant mana and a clever monster as its master."
"Humans cannot be dungeon masters."
"A dungeon's core can be an artifact; taking it stops spawning and disperses the spawns."
"The Night Order's blight dungeon off Abylport was cored by a corrupted Divine bracelet."
"A skinweaver, a tier 5 shapeshifter, was meant to be that dungeon's master; it is dead."
"The Order dreams of 'apocalypse dungeons' that would pour corrupted monsters on the land."
"A proto-dungeon is a lasting magical space made by sacrificing life force."
"Under Thalasarra a sealed air proto-dungeon held the undead Fallen Heroes and a Divine pearl."
"When the Black Abyss Pearl was taken, that proto-dungeon collapsed and flooded; it is dead."
"Renir fears the Divine water glimmercore could turn a whole ocean into a blight dungeon."
"Cyene's Area F guardian, the Cave Badger, was corrupted and purified; it has a glimmerstone eye."
"Renir's amber gem may itself have come out of a dungeon."
